\subsection{Gradual Typing in IR}\label{sec:gradual-typing-ir}

Languages with gradual typing (e.g., TypeScript, Python with type hints) require the IR to handle both statically-typed and dynamically-typed values.

\begin{verbatim}
  // Gradual typing in IR:
  // Static: %x : i32 = add i32 %a, %b    // known type, direct operation
  // Dynamic: %y : Any = dynamic_add %c, %d  // unknown type, runtime check

  // Optimization: type specialization for dynamic values
  // If profiling shows %y is always i32:
  //   Insert type guard: if (typeof(%y) == i32) { ... i32 path ... }
  //   else { ... generic path ... }
  //   The i32 path can be optimized with full type information
\end{verbatim}

